79d2e1:8fb3dbc6-8392-5b83-3871-3f269f2dcb31" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="8fb3dbc6-8392-5b83-3871-3f269f2dcb31" data-wf-component-context="%5B%7B%22componentId%22%3A%228fb3dbc6-8392-5b83-3871-3f269f2dcad6%22%2C%22instanceId%22%3A%227162a65e-2ab0-c598-fa13-46011879d2e1%22%7D%5D" class="button is-footer w-button" value="Send"/></div></form><div class="form_message-success w-form-done"><div>Thank you! Your submission has been received!</div></div><div class="form_message-error w-form-fail"><div>Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.</div></div></div></div></nav><div class="spacer-large adjust"></div><div class="footer_info"><div class="text-size-tiny footer-disclaimer fg-copy"><strong>Primary Regulatory Status: </strong>OMeT-SEF LLC has applied for registration with the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission as a Swap Execution Facility. The application remains pending.<br/>‍<br/><strong>Compliance &amp; Audit Callout: </strong>Execution on the OMeT platform is rules-based. Every transaction is recorded  to the &quot;Waterfall&quot; audit trail to satisfy SEF recordkeeping and transparency mandates.<br/>‍<br/><strong>Institutional Access Boundary:</strong> Access is restricted to Eligible Contract Participants (ECPs). Services are not intended for retail distribution. All trades are mandatorily cleared and settled via integrated Central Counterparties (CCPs) including CME, LCH, and Asigna.<strong>‍<br/></strong></div></div><div class="text-size-tiny">© 2026 OM<em>e</em>T-SEF LLC . All rights reserved. eMOD®, ORP, OMP, OMM  are protected proprietary protocols of OMeT.</div></div></div></div></footer></div><script src="https://d3e54v103j8qbb.cloudfront.net/js/jquery-3.5.1.min.dc5e7f18c8.js?site=69ebd279300b1e4313bac81a" type="text/javascript" integrity="sha256-9/aliU8dGd2tb6OSsuzixeV4y/faTqgFtohetphbbj0=" crossorigin="anonymous"></script><script src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/69ebd279300b1e4313bac81a/js/webflo